        <p>BRIDGE STREET, WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>Church Notices.</p>
        <p>WY CLI F F E CONGREGATIONAL CHURCH, BEWSEY-ST., WARRINGTON. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY). NOV. 14th, 1915. 10.30 a.m. 6.30 p.m. ' Rev. PROFESSOR ARMITAGE, M.A. P.S.A. FOR MEN at 3 p.m.</p>
        <p>WYCLIFFE P.S.A., BEWSEY-STREET. TEMPERANCE SUNDAY, TO-MORROW, NOVEMBER 14th. OPEN MEETING. Programme provided by the Warrington Band of Hope Union. Chair to be taken at 3 o'clock by Mrs. JAMES DODDS, of Penketh. Speaker: Mr. G. ROYLE, Ashton-on-Mersey. Come and Spend a Happy Hour. BOLD-STREET WESLEYAN CHURCH. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), NOV. 14th. Morning, 10.30: Rev. H. T. DIXON. Evening, 6.30: Rev. P. INESON. Subject: "The Great Sacrifice." (2) "The Chosen Fast." Anthem: " I Waited for the Lord" (Mendelssohn).</p>
        <p>Tif 3WSEY-ROAD 'WESLEYAN CHURCH. JIL. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), NOV. 14th. MISSIONARY ANNIVERSARY. Morning, 10.30: Rev. W. T. DERRY, M.A. Evening, 6.30: Rev. 0. J. GRIFFIN. MONDAY, 8 o'clock. PUBLIC MEETING. Deputation: Rev. 0. J. GRIFFIN, West. Africa. Chairman: Mr. ISAAC BARLOW. BAPTIST CHURCH, LATCHFORD. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), NOV. 14th.</p>
        <p>Morning, 10.30. Evening, 6. Preacher: Rev. E. T. DAVIES, Rhyl</p>
        <p>CAIRO-STREET CHAPEL, WARRINGTON. SUNDAY, NOVEMBER 14th. Preacher: Rev. 'IRVINE LISTER. Morning, 10.30. Evening, 6.30.</p>
        <p>CEIRIST CHURCH, LATCHFORD. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), NOV. 14th. 10.45 a.m.: Rev. CANON MORLEY STEVENSON. 6.30 p.m.: The VICAR. Collections for Sunday. School Fund. O.HRISTADELPHIAN MEETING ROOM, le—/ BOLD-STREET, WARRINGTON.—Free Bible Address SUNDAY ' NEXT, at 6.30 On. Subject: The Desire of all Nations." Mr. C. MORRIS, of Stockport. Cl OLBORNE STREET BAPTIST CHURCH. XX TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), NOV. 14th. Preacher: Rev. H. OGDEN. Morning, 10.45: "The Limits Of Liberty." Evening, 6.46: "The Church and Temperance." Soloist: Mr. JOSEPH POOLE. PRIAUTIVE METHODIST CHURCH, LEGH-STREET, WARRINGTON, TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), NOV. 14th, s 1915. TEMPERANCE SUNDAY. Preacher: Rev. A. J. CHESSUM. Morning, 10.30. Evening, 6.30.</p>
        <p>_ REFORMED CHURCH OF ENGLAND, EMMANUEL CHURCH, BOLD-STREET, Services every SUNDAY, at 10.20 a.m. &amp; 6.30"p.m. Rev. W. T. JAYE, Incumbent. The Church provides a distinctly Protesta.iat Church of England service. All Seats Free.</p>
        <p>QT. JOHN'S PRESBYTERIAN -CHURCH, ).7 WILDERSPOOL CAUSEWAY. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY). NOV. 14th, 1915. Morning, 10.45. Evenirtz, 6.30. Preacher: Rev. W. REID.</p>
        <p>Public Notices.</p>
        <p>_TOSEPH CROSFIELD &amp; SONS, LIMITED. GP 4i PER CENT. IST MORTGAGE DEBENTURE STOCK. The Transfer Books of this Company relative to this issue will be CLOSED from the 17th to '36th November (both days inclusive) for the purpose of preparing and issuing Interest Warrants, due let December. (Signed) GILES HUNT, Secretary. Warrington, 9th November. 1916.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON SECONDARY SCHOOL OLD BOYS' CHRISTMAS FUND.</p>
        <p>The PRINCIPAL will be glad to receive SUBSCRIPTIONS from Past Pupils and Friends of the School to the Fund providing a.</p>
        <p>SMALL CHRISTMAS GIFT TO EACif OLD BOY serving with His Majesty's Forces.</p>
        <p>A NCIEIT ORDER OF t'Ultt _LAU). WARRINGTON DISTAICT.</p>
        <p>All MeMbere are cordia,4y invited to accompany HIS WORSHIP THE MAYOR, Alderman Brother Peter. Peacock, to the PARISH CHURCH on SUNDAY MORNING, 14th inst. ' Assemble in front of Town Hall, 9.45 a.m. prompt. Regalia to be. worn. E. R. HOLLINS. D.C.R.</p>
        <p>WARINGTON BAND OF HOPE UNION TEMPERANCE. SUNDAY, TO-MORROW, NOVEMBER 14th. PUBLIC MEETING IN THE CO-OPERATIVE HALL. Addresses by Rev. W. REID and Rev. A. j. MORTON. MUSICAL ITEMS by the UNITED CHOIR. Chair to be taken at 8.15 p.m. by Mrs. JAMES DODDS. COLLECTION.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON MUSICAL SOCIETY. V'V President: Sir Gilbert Greenall, Bart., C.V.O. GRAND PATRIOTIC CONCERT IN PARR HALL, SATURDAY, NOV. 27th, In aid of Local War Funds. Edward (Ferman's " MERRIE ENGLAND" (Concert Version), By permission of Messrs. Chappell and Co. Principals: Mde. SARA SILCOCK, Miss HELEN ANDERTON, Mr. J. RABBITT, Mr. J. W. BIBBY. FULL CHORUS AND ORCHESTRA. Conductor: Mr. FRANK ,H. CROSSLEY. Leader of Orchestra: Mr. R. H. PEARSON. Accompanist: Mr. W. H. PAYTON, Mus.Bac. Doors open 7.0. Commence 7.30. Carriages 10 p.m. Ticket-holders admitted by early door at 6.45. Prices of Admission: 35., 25., and is. 6d., Reserved; is. and 6d., Unreserved. The Plan of Reserved Seats is now open to sub- scribers, and will be opened to the general public on and after Saturday next, Nov. 20th, at Mr. Pear- son's Bridge-at., where tickets for the unreserved seats may also be had; tickets for unreserved seats may also be obtained at Messrs. Dawson's, Sankey- st., and from any Member of the Musical Society. LIONEL FAIRCLOUGH. Hon. Sec.</p>
        <p>WAR RINCI TON INSURANCE COMMITTEE. CHANGE OF DOCTOR.</p>
        <p>Any insured person, within the area of the War- rington Insurance Committee, who desires to be attended, after the 31st December next, by a doctor other than the doctor from whom he is entitled to obtain treatment during the current year. must give notice to the Committee BEFORE THE IST DECEMBER NEXT. Such notice must be in writing (signed by the insured person), and must be accompanied by the Medical Card.</p>
        <p>Insured persons on the list of a doctor holding a Commission in the Army or Navy will not be entitled to change their doctor at the end of the year unless they satisfy the Medical Service Sub- committee that they have reasonable grounds for desiring to change, in which case they must send to me, along with their medical card, a full state- ment of the reasons on which the application to choose another doctor is based.</p>
        <p>Dated this 12th day of November, 1915. ALFRED TILLING, Clerk to the Committee. Trinity Chambers, Market Gate, Warrington.</p>
        <p>No. 1,816.</p>
