      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1915-11-13_WidnesExaminer_art0060" n="art0060">
        <head>DARDANELLES.</head>
        <p>DARDANELLES.</p>
        <p>Post Office Notice. I</p>
        <p>The postal authorities on 'Tuesday ,issued a notice of the conditions which will -govern the dispatch of Christmas mails for the Mediter- ranean Expeditionary Force. in view of the special difficultiv atending their-titisnsmission, the public are requested to limit the use of the parcel post strictly to articles of real utility. .Perishable articles and bottles, pudding basins, and the like will not be accepted for trans- mission, and as from November 11th the maxi- mum weight for a Single parcel will be reduced to seven pounds, parcels should be carefully packed .and as nearly round as• possible, well padded, and wrapped in waterproof paper. Parcels which do not comply with that and other conditions indicated are unlikely to reach their destination safely, and those.- which do not show the name and address of the sender on ,the cover will be refused. •</p>
        <p>To secure delivery on or before Christmas Day, letters should be potted not later than December Ist, and parcels, not later than -November 16th. All letters and .parcels for the troops must be fully and completely addressed in bold letters in ink or indelible pencil, and those for men in hospital should, where the actual hospital is not known, bear the word " hospital " in large printed characters.</p>
        <p>SAVING TIME.</p>
        <p>C,/4</p>
        <p>Council Committees Not To</p>
        <p>Mect Fo N3th]ng.</p>
      </div>
