        <p>, Mrs. W. Cook, Railway Cottages, St. John's, Woking, writes. "Sloan's Liniment has done me more good than anyother prepara tion I have tried. It is marvellous for relieving pain. I have neve: known anything to relieve pain so quickly." Mr. J. T. Harvey, 276 High Street, Glasgow. writes :—" I consid, Sloan's Liniment has no equal. In my home we have success!' used it for sprained wrists and stiff neck. In both cases it curer like magic.' Sloan's Liniment is the finest remedy for Rheu. matism, Sciatica, Lumbago, Sprains. Bruises and any kind of pain. It penetrates by itself—no rub. bing is required. Sold by all chemists, 1/11 and 2/3. Send your name and address FREE ,AMPLE postage of trial bottle FREE. Wholesale Depot: 86. Clerk,</p>
