        <p>Public Notices. BRITISH AND FOREIGN BIBLE SOCIETY. WARRINGTON AUXILIARY. THE ANNUAL MEETING will be held on THURSDAY EVENING, NOVEMBER 25th, 1915, In the CO-OPERATIVE HALL. CAIRO-STREET. HIS WORSHIP THE MAYOR will preside. The Rev. H. C. MOORE, Vicar of Earlestown, and the Rev. TOM DRING (newly-appointed Dis- trict Secretary) will address the meeting.</p>
        <p>Warrington E. I. Co-operative Society Ld• The 220th QUARTERLY MEETING will be held in the CO-OPERATIVE HALL, CAIRO ST., On MONDAY, NOVEMBER 22nd, 1915, at 8 p.m. Members must produce their Membership Card and Dividend Warrant or Pass Book, or they cannot be admitted or allowed to vote. SPECIAL BUSINESS. Nominated. ELECTION OF COMMITTEE BERRY, FRANK. HALEY, G. (Three required). CLEGG, W. E. *SIIERBURN, W. H. *Retiring Members eligible for re-election. ENGLAND, E. *WRIGHT, W. LORD DERBY'S RECRUITING CAMPAIGN. A statement will be made respecting our employes, and resolutions submitted as to allowances, &amp;c. At the close of General Business THE MEETING WILL BE DECLARED SPECIAL For the consideration and adoption (or otherwise) of Proposals for Alteration of Rules. For particulars see Balance Sheet. DIVIDENDS will be paid according to the dates on back of Dividend Warrants, beginning November 30th.</p>
        <p>Public Notices. nnHE CORPORATION OF WARRINGTON .I. is prepared to receive LOANS either for six months' notice or for a term of years. Applications, stating amount for investment, to be made to the Borough Treasurer, Municipal Offices, Warrington. SCHOOL Secretaries everywhere should engage • FELIX MILLS, Entertainer, Oldham, to ex- hibit his Pictorial Tour, " Aczoss Europe with the British Army." Record audiences. Particulars free. LORD —DERBY WAR HOSPITAL. It is proposed to hold a " TOMMIES' " TEA in the PARR HALL on the 9th .DECEMBER, to pro- vide a permanent Cinematograph for the use of the above institution, and Comforts for the inmates. Visitors to the Hospital, and those interested, are cordially invited td attend a Meeting in the Town Hall on Tuesday evening next, at 8 o'clock. H. B. HOUGHTON Hon. Sec. H. J. WESTBROOIe, Hon, Treas.</p>
