        <p>LOCAL INTELLIGENCE. Fellow Workers' Sympathy. At a meeting of the 'Warrington Trades and Labour Council on Tuesday night, a vote af syMpathy was passed with Mr. F. Bell. of the Railway Workers' Union, who has mat with an accident, and is at present lying in the Infirmary. Licence Changes Hands. At the Borough Police Court on Monday, the juEitices granted to Mr. Walter Richard Smith the temporary transfer of the licence of the Victoria Vaults, Mersey-street. The application was made by Mr. Arthur Browne.</p>
