        <p>Mr. and Mrs. Vavid Renshaw, 168, Longford- street, Warrington, have received news from an unofficial source that their son, Private John David Renshaw, is missing. Sergeant Widocks's Version. The first intimation was received by a sister of the above Private (Mrs. Jackson, caretaker of the Bolton Council School) from Sergeant E. J. Widocks, who, on Thursday of last week, in reply to a communication from his parents, wrote the following letter : " Dear Mrs. Jackson,—l received your very kind letter, and I very much regret that I cannot give you ant' good -news. It is no use in holding out any hope to you where none exists. I know Jack was in the dug-out with the two that got killed, and the dug-out got knocked in. They were all buried beneath the debris, and owing to the darkness and the mud, &amp;c., no one could definitely, say just what happened. Any way, all the bodies that the stretcher-bearers found the next day were all</p>
