        <p>PRIVATE JOHN GRUNDY.</p>
        <p>Ltd., having worked there since leaving school. He rejoined the Territorials at the outbreak of war, having previously served in them for a considerable time. His brother, Lance-Corporal Grundy, also of the Territorials, was wounded on June 11th, and is now at home recuperating. • PRIVATE A. SHARP. -- Leg Injury And Eye Damaged By Gas. Private Arthur Sharp, of the Warrington Territorials, whose home address is 288. Win- wick-road, has been wounded in the calf of the left leg, and has had his eye affected by gas. 1. Private Sharp is a native of Earlestown, hav- ing attended schod there and worked at the Vulcan Works. He has belonged to the Terri- torials for several years, and rejoined them at the outbreak of war.</p>
